{
  "format": "genereti-guide",
  "version": 1,
  "id": "shader-buffers",
  "title": "Livecode: shader buffers and history",
  "summary": "Connected GLSL passes, one-frame history and an explicit fresh/history composite.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Make fresh ink",
      "text": "The first GLSL node paints moving RGB ink. Each Livecode node is a separate render pass. Change speed without rebuilding the shader.",
      "target": {
        "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
        "ref": "2d8ba61b-2075-59a0-ac0b-0c1c895cb38a",
        "part": "node"
      },
      "hint": "mainImage, iTime, iResolution and iChannel0 aliases are supported. Annotated float speed becomes a regular parameter and controls.value0 socket.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "set-widget",
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "2d8ba61b-2075-59a0-ac0b-0c1c895cb38a",
            "widget": "controls.value0",
            "part": "parameter"
          },
          "value": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reference the end of the loop",
      "text": "Buffer A reads the previous composite. Its optional IMAGE input seeds frame one; it does not choose the history target. Pick the combine node in reference.",
      "target": {
        "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureFeedbackRef",
        "ref": "bd44969b-52fe-5e13-9d83-d40d4d0e5156",
        "part": "node"
      },
      "hint": "Fresh → composite; previous composite → warp/fade → composite. The reference closes the loop with a one-tick delay, so there is no cyclic IMAGE wire.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "set-widget",
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureFeedbackRef",
            "ref": "bd44969b-52fe-5e13-9d83-d40d4d0e5156",
            "widget": "reference",
            "part": "parameter"
          },
          "value": "{\"ref\":\"7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786\",\"outputSlot\":0}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Process the history buffer",
      "text": "The warp pass samples its IMAGE input as iChannel0 / u_image. It rotates, expands and fades yesterday’s pixels before they reach the composite.",
      "target": {
        "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
        "ref": "a7f55850-adf1-5de0-ba67-7f6407613f1e",
        "part": "node"
      },
      "hint": "Lower decay shortens trails. Here one input is one external buffer; internal Shadertoy A–D/Common tabs and four channel inputs are not implemented.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "set-widget",
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "a7f55850-adf1-5de0-ba67-7f6407613f1e",
            "widget": "controls.value0",
            "part": "parameter"
          },
          "value": 0.9
        },
        {
          "kind": "connect",
          "source": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureFeedbackRef",
            "ref": "bd44969b-52fe-5e13-9d83-d40d4d0e5156"
          },
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "a7f55850-adf1-5de0-ba67-7f6407613f1e"
          },
          "input": "image",
          "output": "image"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Combine fresh and old frames",
      "text": "Add fresh RGB ink to faded history. Display grading comes after the composite so it cannot amplify history each tick.",
      "target": {
        "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureComposite",
        "ref": "7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786",
        "part": "node"
      },
      "hint": "Screen is another useful blend. Over with an opaque black source would hide history. Do it restores additive routing.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "set-widget",
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureComposite",
            "ref": "7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786",
            "widget": "operation",
            "part": "parameter"
          },
          "value": "add"
        },
        {
          "kind": "connect",
          "source": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "2d8ba61b-2075-59a0-ac0b-0c1c895cb38a"
          },
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureComposite",
            "ref": "7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786"
          },
          "input": "image",
          "output": "IMAGE"
        },
        {
          "kind": "connect",
          "source": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "a7f55850-adf1-5de0-ba67-7f6407613f1e"
          },
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureComposite",
            "ref": "7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786"
          },
          "input": "background",
          "output": "IMAGE"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Finish and interact",
      "text": "Increase contrast in the Image pass. Alt+W opens the actual interactive preview; Shift-click its overlay button or Alt+O keeps only the node output.",
      "target": {
        "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
        "ref": "70f0113e-c398-50f4-84a2-0767426c824c",
        "part": "node"
      },
      "hint": "IMAGE between Livecode nodes crosses separate browser runtimes. TOP operators keep their own GPU chain. Use dat.monitor on your actual patch rather than assuming a fixed frame rate.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "set-widget",
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "70f0113e-c398-50f4-84a2-0767426c824c",
            "widget": "controls.value0",
            "part": "parameter"
          },
          "value": 1.6
        },
        {
          "kind": "connect",
          "source": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiTextureComposite",
            "ref": "7c1d94b6-8bb6-5f37-ac14-c7902efee786"
          },
          "target": {
            "nodeType": "GeneretiLivecode",
            "ref": "70f0113e-c398-50f4-84a2-0767426c824c"
          },
          "input": "image",
          "output": "image"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

